{
  "closure_notes": [
    "Preserve the physical inputs tree exactly. The loader rejects extra or missing frozen files except __pycache__.",
    "The selected-result.json compatibility path accepts only either of two complete byte records; no source-pin bypass is needed.",
    "Native Catalogue and adapter import pr589-five-helper-hosting/verify.py for exact rational matrix/projector functions. That file is already one of the 12 SOURCES entries; its default old word/host/geometry files are also included by the loader authentication.",
    "The fixed-slot proof precedent verify.py is hashed for exact attribution/proof lineage but not executed, so its own data dependencies are not part of this replay closure.",
    "Both interval engines are self-contained standard-library modules.",
    "build_word_pool35.py imports the adapter only for pure lower_word; full adapter.load additionally uses the retained physical tree and authenticated live inputs.",
    "block_prefix_word.py calls block_prefix.block_audit and checks the candidate idle inventory equals the original pool35 inventory; both must remain bundled.",
    "Geometry --candidate paths should be absolute when source manifests are emitted. The frozen fixed_slot_ceiling.py and block_prefix_word.py do not normalize relative candidate paths before Path.relative_to; the parent wrapper resolves them.",
    "All output paths must be fresh. Internal scope files under research/kappa-next-regime are bundled by the parent release."
  ],
